# Use events from another API

Add the API as a project dependency, run `trellis update`, then select the event in the participant:

```trellis
participant "acme.notifications@v1" service {
  implements "acme.notifications@v1";
  use required orders "acme.orders@v1" {
    subscribe event "Orders.Shipped";
  }
}
```

`trellis generate` emits the selected descriptor and records the exact referenced API digest in the participant artifact.

This consumer owns a separate notifications API and depends on the Orders API
from the previous step. Register `service.onOrdersShipped(...)` during startup,
not inside an RPC handler. Read the typed payload from the handler's `event`
argument and return a `Result` after processing it.

Keep handlers idempotent when delivery can repeat. If a non-idempotent SQL side
effect needs duplicate suppression, commit its inbox marker in the same
transaction as that side effect. A runtime-delivered event is already proof
verified; do not reconstruct signatures or bypass generated subscriptions with
raw transport listeners.
